<h3><font color=#cc0f14>Exercises related to the ALFALFA observing
mode</font></h3>

Review the 
<a href="http://www.astro.cornell.edu/~galaxy/docs/figbeams.pdf">
memo</a> we wrote on ALFA beam rotation.</p>

Suppose the ALFALFA schedule for a given day (see February 8, 2007 at the
team <a href="http://www.naic.edu/~a2010/scheds/a2010_schedspr07.txt">
http://www.naic.edu/~a2010/scheds/a2010_schedspr07.txt</a> schedule page)
targets the drift at +28d35'30"; therefore, the central beam 
(designated Beam "0") is the one
which is set to declination of +28d35'30".</p> 

<ol>
<li> What is the zenith angle of this drift as observed with ALFA beam
0?

<li>

<li> List the resultant seven declinations covered by
the seven beams, in order, from south to north.

<li> Assuming a mean effective HPBW of the telescope at 1.4 GHz 
(the frequency of the HI line) is about 3.5 arcminutes, how long does
it take for a source to traverse the beam?
</ol>

<br>
